        "summary": "Fixed the NOT_NULL rule false positive for CREATE INDEX with WHERE clause containing IS NOT NULL.\n\nThe fix added `and not sql.startswith(\"CREATE INDEX\")` to the condition in `has_not_null_column()` function in `django_migration_linter/sql_analyser/base.py` line 46. This excludes CREATE INDEX statements from the NOT_NULL detection, while still correctly detecting actual NOT NULL constraints on columns via ALTER TABLE statements.\n\nAll 37 tests in test_sql_analyser.py pass, including the specific test `test_create_index_concurrently_where` that was failing before the fix.",
